Lunacy's Android Notifications.

With Lunacy as Android's home screen, Android's own notification shade is out of sight. This
app shows Android's notifications the webOS way: one dashboard per Android app, its
notifications stacked as the dashboard's layers, with a banner for the ones Android ranks as
urgent. It has no window of its own; Lunacy starts it when there is something to show, and it
ends when the last of its dashboards goes.

The notifications come from palm://org.webosarchive.lunacy/android/notifications, which
Lunacy only answers for its own apps, and only once the owner has allowed Lunacy to read
Android's notifications on Android's Notification access screen. They are kept in memory
while Android has them, and never written down or sent anywhere.

The app's code is Lunacy's, under the same terms as the rest of Lunacy. Its dashboards are
Enyo's own (enyo.Dashboard); it carries no art of its own.
